{
  "id": "fluency-l9-products-quotients",
  "lesson": "l9-products-quotients",
  "title": "Fluency: products and quotients",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "product-rule",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "differentiate a product",
      "vars": {
        "n": { "int": [2, 6] },
        "a": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "b": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": { "n1": "n - 1", "na": "n*a", "nb": "n*b", "top": "(n + 1)*a" },
      "prompt": "Use the product rule to differentiate $f(x) = x^{n}({a:c}x{b:+})$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{top}x^{{{n}}}{nb:+}{mono(x; 1, n1)}", "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "product-of-derivatives", "tex": "{mono(x; na, n1)}", "line": "You multiplied the two derivatives. The product rule is $u'v + uv'$." },
        { "id": "one-term-only", "tex": "{na}x^{{{n}}}{nb:+}{mono(x; 1, n1)}", "line": "You kept $u'v$ but left out $uv'$, the term from the bracket's slope." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Take $u = x^{n}$ and $v = {a:c}x{b:+}$, so $u' = {mono(x; n, n1)}$ and $v' = {a}$.",
        "$u'v + uv' = {mono(x; n, n1)}({a:c}x{b:+}){a:+c}x^{n}$.",
        "Multiply out and collect: $f'(x) = {top}x^{{{n}}}{nb:+}{mono(x; 1, n1)}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "quotient-rule",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "differentiate a quotient",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] },
        "b": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "c": { "int": [1, 5] },
        "d": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": { "top": "a*d - b*c", "rev": "b*c - a*d", "sg": "sign(a*d - b*c)", "mag": "abs(a*d - b*c)" },
      "where": ["a*d - b*c != 0", "gcd(abs(a), abs(b)) == 1", "gcd(c, abs(d)) == 1"],
      "prompt": "Use the quotient rule to differentiate $f(x) = \\dfrac{{{a:c}x{b:+}}}{{{c:c}x{d:+}}}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{sg:c}\\frac{{{mag}}}{{({c:c}x{d:+})^2}}", "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "sign-reversed", "tex": "\\frac{{{rev}}}{{({c:c}x{d:+})^2}}", "line": "You worked out $uv' - u'v$. The quotient rule is $\\dfrac{{u'v - uv'}}{{v^2}}$." },
        { "id": "not-squared", "tex": "\\frac{{{top}}}{{{c:c}x{d:+}}}", "line": "You forgot to square the bottom: divide by $v^2$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Take $u = {a:c}x{b:+}$ and $v = {c:c}x{d:+}$, so $u' = {a}$ and $v' = {c}$.",
        "The top is $u'v - uv' = {a:()}({c:c}x{d:+}) - {c:c}({a:c}x{b:+}) = {top}$.",
        "So $f'(x) = {sg:c}\\dfrac{{{mag}}}{{({c:c}x{d:+})^2}}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "product-at-a-point",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "find the slope of a product at a point",
      "vars": {
        "p": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "q": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] },
        "r": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "k": { "int": [-3, 3], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": {
        "uk": "k^2 + p", "vk": "q*k + r", "duk": "2*k",
        "s": "2*k*(q*k + r) + (k^2 + p)*q",
        "pd": "2*k*q", "one": "2*k*(q*k + r)"
      },
      "where": ["pd != s", "one != s", "pd != one"],
      "prompt": "Take $f(x) = (x^2{p:+})({q:c}x{r:+})$. Work out $f'({k})$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{s}", "tol": { "abs": 0 } },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "product-of-derivatives", "value": "{pd}", "line": "You multiplied the two derivatives. The product rule is $u'v + uv'$." },
        { "id": "one-term-only", "value": "{one}", "line": "You kept $u'v$ but left out $uv'$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "At $x = {k}$: $u = {uk}$, $u' = {duk}$, $v = {vk}$ and $v' = {q}$.",
        "$f'({k}) = u'v + uv' = {duk:()} \\times {vk:()} + {uk:()} \\times {q:()} = {s}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
